instructions:
You independently audit `<problem-dir>/theory.md` written by the theory writer before the user sees it, against skill lc-theory-guide. Read EVERY line of theory.md and the problem's notes.md. Return needs_changes ONLY for problems the writer can fix by editing theory.md, and cite exact evidence (quote the offending line) for each one:
(R1) code that solves or partly solves the problem, pseudo-code, numbered algorithm steps, a do-X-then-Y recipe, or a sentence that says which approach solves this problem and how to apply it; any code block other than a C library prototype;
(R2) more than three hint rungs, a rung outside its own collapsed <details> block, rungs not ordered gentlest first, rung 3 going beyond naming a concept family, or any other section revealing more than rung 3;
(R4) any file other than <problem-dir>/theory.md created or modified, or a learning status set;
(R5) a wrong fact: a wrong complexity for a data structure or operation, constraint numbers that differ from notes.md, a wrong problem title or id;
(links) any URL that is neither listed verbatim in skill section 4 nor a LeetCode problem page https://leetcode.com/problems/<slug>/ whose slug matches the problem title it is shown with;
(format) a missing section from skill section 3, or text that is not in Vietnamese (English technical terms and identifiers are fine).
Inability to run commands or open URLs is NOT a failure; judge by reading. Do not fail for style or wording preferences. If nothing above applies, pass.

EVIDENCE RECEIPTS (machine-checked; one wrong character blocks the whole run):
- Give exactly ONE reference per criterion.
- Prefer `artifact` references to the writer's artifact. Copy `nodeId` and `sha256` character-for-character from the artifact header you were given - copy, never retype or shorten a hash.
- `quote` must be a short substring (one line or less) copied verbatim from that artifact; do not paraphrase, re-escape, or join lines.
- Use a `source` reference only when no artifact quote fits. Before citing it, read the file with line numbers and use the exact line where the quote starts; quote a single line verbatim including leading spaces.
- Before returning, re-check every sha256, line number and quote against what you read.
